{
  "providerId": "dodomain.io",
  "providerName": "DoDomain",
  "serviceId": "record-set",
  "serviceName": "Custom DNS record set",
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Applies the DNS records a SaaS product needs to connect a customer's domain when they do not fit one of DoDomain's fixed templates (several CNAMEs and TXTs for an email provider, MX for inbound mail, SRV for a service, CAA for certificate issuance). The template is a pool of typed slots; each slot is its own group, and every apply names exactly the groups it fills via groupId, so only the records shown on the consent screen are written. TTL is fixed at 3600. Record types are fixed per slot. Every apply is signed (syncPubKeyDomain), so only DoDomain's server can choose the values. Used by DoDomain (domain-connect-as-a-service) on behalf of its integrator applications.",
  "variableDescription": "Every variable name is lowercase. Each slot is group <type><n> (a1-a8, aaaa1-aaaa4, cname1-cname16, txt1-txt8, mx1-mx5, srv1-srv4, ns1-ns4, caa1-caa2) and its variables are named <type><number in words><field>, e.g. group cname16 uses %cnamesixteenhost%. Each slot has: %<slot>host% = record label relative to the apply host ('@' for the apex); %<slot>value% = record value (IPv4, IPv6, target host, TXT content, MX/NS host, or CAA value); MX and SRV slots add %<slot>priority%; SRV slots use %<slot>name% (label), %<slot>service% (with the leading underscore, e.g. _sip), %<slot>weight%, %<slot>port%, %<slot>target%; the SRV protocol is fixed per slot (srv1 and srv2 _tcp, srv3 _udp, srv4 _tls); CAA slots add %<slot>tag% (issue, issuewild or iodef). %spfmrules% = the SPF mechanisms merged into the zone's existing SPF record (group spfm). DoDomain never sends '@' for an NS or CNAME slot.",
  "syncBlock": false,
  "hostRequired": false,
  "multiInstance": true,
  "syncPubKeyDomain": "dckeys.dodomain.io",
  "syncRedirectDomain": "app.dodomain.io",
